+# The Daily Grind
+
+Coffee shop site with passkey-based customer accounts at `/account`.
+
+```sh
+pnpm install
+pnpm start   # http://localhost:11222
+pnpm test
+```
+
+## Passkeys
+
+Customers create an account, sign in, and confirm sensitive actions with passkeys (WebAuthn) — there
+are no passwords. The server lives in `server/` and uses
+[SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev); the UI is `public/account.html` + `public/assets/account.js`.
+
+- **Create an account** with a name, email, and a new discoverable passkey.
+- **Sign in** with the passkey button or straight from the email field's autofill menu.
+- **Manage passkeys**: add (one per device/password manager), rename, remove. The last passkey can't be
+  removed, and removing one signs out the account's other sessions.
+- **Profile**: update name and email.
+- **Reauthentication**: changing email, adding a passkey, and removing a passkey require a passkey
+  verification within the last 5 minutes; otherwise the UI asks the customer to confirm it's them.
+- Uses the WebAuthn Signal API (where supported) so password managers hide removed passkeys and
+  show updated names/emails.
+
+### Configuration
+
+| Variable      | Default                  | Notes                                                     |
+| ------------- | ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `PORT`        | `11222`                  |                                                           |
+| `ORIGIN`      | `http://localhost:$PORT` | Exact origin customers use. Must be `https` in production. |
+| `RP_ID`       | hostname of `ORIGIN`     | e.g. `dailygrind.coffee`. Passkeys are bound to it — don't change it later. |
+| `DATA_FILE`   | `data/db.json`           | JSON account store.                                       |
+| `TRUST_PROXY` | unset                    | Set when behind a reverse proxy so rate limiting uses `X-Forwarded-For`. |
+
+Sessions are kept in memory, so restarting the server signs everyone out.
